  "finding": "Pinned source contains no implicit AUT stop, clear-state or relaunch in separate CLI session startup/cleanup. Each command recreates Maestro driver connections; AUT lifecycle commands are explicit flow operations.",
  "chains": {
    "entry": "TestCommand.kt:477-500 -> MaestroSessionManager.newSession -> shutdown hook at119-131 -> session.close -> Maestro.close -> driver.close",
    "android": "AndroidDriver.kt:112-149,170-200 installs/starts/closes only Maestro instrumentation and transport. AndroidDeviceConnection.kt:278-299 closes its shell stream/gRPC/ADB connection.",
    "ios": "IOSDriver.kt:92-108 -> ios/LocalIOSDevice.kt:150-152 -> XCTestIOSDevice.kt:196-198 -> XCTestDriverClient.kt:223-225 -> LocalXCTestInstaller.kt:244-255 -> SimctlIOSDevice.kt:197-203. The sole stopped/uninstalled bundle in this cleanup is dev.mobile.maestro-driver-iosUITests.xctrunner.",
    "flow": "Orchestra.kt:199-268 runs supplied commands and only configured onFlowStart/onFlowComplete hooks. The production QA capture flow has no launchApp/stopApp/clearState; it opens the explicit QA capture deep-link.",
    "junit": "TestSuiteInteractor maps successful flow to FlowStatus.SUCCESS; JUnitTestSuiteReporter serializes this enum; its pinned test expects status=SUCCESS."
  },
  "orderedAlternative": "Pinned TestSuiteInteractor.kt:71-90 supports explicitly ordered flows with continueOnFailure=true in one session if future platform evidence requires avoiding driver restart. Not required by current source review.",
  "limits": [
    "Read-only official pinned source review, not a device experiment or decompilation of the release ZIP.",
    "Driver restart can change which app is foreground; capture openLink reactivates the AUT. No claim that OS can never evict a background app.",
    "Cumulative fixture, account readback, capture and full-app verification must remain mandatory so any process/state loss fails acceptance.",
    "Official current sequential-execution docs recommend isolated flows; this specific cumulative QA sequence is deliberately validated against the pinned source and must pass its native rerun."
  ]
}
